      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can make this change in `ec_cmd_api.h`\n```\ndiff --git a/include/ec_cmd_api.h b/include/ec_cmd_api.h\nindex cb1522aea6..b01ca43c14 100644\n--- a/include/ec_cmd_api.h\n+++ b/include/ec_cmd_api.h\n@@ -306,7 +306,7 @@ _CROS_EC_C0_F_PF_RF(EC_CMD_FP_READ_MATCH_SECRET, fp_read_match_secret);\n\n-_CROS_EC_CV_F_R(EC_CMD_FP_INFO, 1, fp_info, fp_info);\n+_CROS_EC_CV_F_R(EC_CMD_FP_INFO, 2, fp_info, fp_info_v2);\n```\nwhich will expand to the following:\n\n```\nstatic inline int ec_cmd_fp_info(CROS_EC_COMMAND_INFO *h,\n\t\t\t\t struct ec_response_fp_info_v2 *r)\n{\n\treturn CROS_EC_COMMAND(h, (EC_CMD_FP_INFO), (2), NULL, 0, r,\n\t\t\t       sizeof(*r));\n}\n```\n\nI can now try to use the modified `ec_cmd_fp_info` macro inside `zephyr/test/fingerprint/task/src/fpsensor_init.cc`\n\n```\ndiff --git a/zephyr/test/fingerprint/task/src/fpsensor_init.cc b/zephyr/test/fingerprint/task/src/fpsensor_init.cc\nindex f529fe286a..9d8c7f294f 100644\n--- a/zephyr/test/fingerprint/task/src/fpsensor_init.cc\n+++ b/zephyr/test/fingerprint/task/src/fpsensor_init.cc\n@@ -127,7 +127,7 @@ ZTEST_USER(fpsensor_init, test_maintenance_mode_dead_pixel_3)\n        const int dead_pixels \u003d 3;\n \n        /* Confirm that number of dead pixels is unknown. */\n-       zassert_ok(fpinfo_cmd_helper(test_info_buffer));\n+       zassert_ok(ec_cmd_fp_info(NULL, test_info_buffer));\n        zassert_equal(\n                FP_ERROR_DEAD_PIXELS(test_info_buffer-\u003esensor_info.errors),\n                FP_ERROR_DEAD_PIXELS_UNKNOWN);\n@@ -148,7 +148,7 @@ ZTEST_USER(fpsensor_init, test_maintenance_mode_dead_pixel_3)\n        zassert_true(state.maintenance_ran);\n \n        /* Confirm that number of dead pixels is correct. */\n-       zassert_ok(fpinfo_cmd_helper(test_info_buffer));\n+       zassert_ok(ec_cmd_fp_info(NULL, test_info_buffer));\n        zassert_equal(\n                FP_ERROR_DEAD_PIXELS(test_info_buffer-\u003esensor_info.errors),\n                dead_pixels);\n@@ -186,7 +186,7 @@ ZTEST_USER(fpsensor_init, test_maintenance_mode_dead_pixel_max_plus_2)\n        zassert_true(state.maintenance_ran);\n \n        /* Confirm that number of dead pixels is correct. */\n-       zassert_ok(fpinfo_cmd_helper(test_info_buffer));\n+       zassert_ok(ec_cmd_fp_info(NULL, test_info_buffer));\n        zassert_equal(\n                FP_ERROR_DEAD_PIXELS(test_info_buffer-\u003esensor_info.errors),\n                FP_ERROR_DEAD_PIXELS_MAX);\n@@ -224,7 +224,7 @@ ZTEST_USER(fpsensor_init, test_maintenance_mode_dead_pixel_max)\n        zassert_true(state.maintenance_ran);\n \n        /* Confirm that number of dead pixels is correct. */\n-       zassert_ok(fpinfo_cmd_helper(test_info_buffer));\n+       zassert_ok(ec_cmd_fp_info(NULL, test_info_buffer));\n        zassert_equal(\n                FP_ERROR_DEAD_PIXELS(test_info_buffer-\u003esensor_info.errors),\n                FP_ERROR_DEAD_PIXELS_MAX);\n@@ -262,7 +262,7 @@ ZTEST_USER(fpsensor_init, test_maintenance_mode_dead_pixel_max_minus_1)\n        zassert_true(state.maintenance_ran);\n \n        /* Confirm that number of dead pixels is correct. */\n-       zassert_ok(fpinfo_cmd_helper(test_info_buffer));\n+       zassert_ok(ec_cmd_fp_info(NULL, test_info_buffer));\n        zassert_equal(\n                FP_ERROR_DEAD_PIXELS(test_info_buffer-\u003esensor_info.errors),\n                FP_ERROR_DEAD_PIXELS_MAX - 1);\n```\n\nThe tests will fail saying that the command returns `err 9`, which I expected to be `EC_RES_UNAVAILABLE` because of the failing comparison between `args-\u003eresponse_max` and the input buffer size. If I make the below change, replacing `args-\u003eresponse_max` by 1000, the tests pass. If I print `args-\u003eresponse_max` from the `common/sensor.cc` during this simulated test, the value is `36`. IIRC, it is `532` in real operation.\n\nIt seems the 36 is coming from the size of `struct ec_response_fp_info_v2`\n\n```\nstruct fp_sensor_info {\n\t/* Sensor identification */\n\tuint32_t vendor_id;\n\tuint32_t product_id;\n\tuint32_t model_id;\n\tuint32_t version;\n\tuint16_t num_capture_types; /* number of image capture types */\n\tuint16_t errors; /* see FP_ERROR_ flags above */\n} __ec_align4;\nBUILD_ASSERT(sizeof(struct fp_sensor_info) \u003d\u003d 20);\n\nstruct fp_template_info {\n\t/* Template/finger current information */\n\tuint32_t template_size; /* max template size in bytes */\n\tuint16_t template_max; /* maximum number of fingers/templates */\n\tuint16_t template_valid; /* number of valid fingers/templates */\n\tuint32_t template_dirty; /* bitmap of templates with MCU side changes */\n\tuint32_t template_version; /* version of the template format */\n} __ec_align4;\nBUILD_ASSERT(sizeof(struct fp_template_info) \u003d\u003d 16);\n```\n\n```\nfsammoura@fsammoura2:~/chromiumos/src/platform/ec$ git diff\ndiff --git a/common/fpsensor/fpsensor.cc b/common/fpsensor/fpsensor.cc\nindex cafc3c3e38..d6a6a54dbb 100644\n--- a/common/fpsensor/fpsensor.cc\n+++ b/common/fpsensor/fpsensor.cc\n@@ -393,7 +393,7 @@ static enum ec_status fp_command_info(struct host_cmd_handler_args *args)\n                static_cast\u003cec_response_fp_info_v2 *\u003e(args-\u003eresponse);\n \n #ifdef HAVE_FP_PRIVATE_DRIVER\n-       if (fp_sensor_get_info(r, args-\u003eresponse_max) \u003c 0)\n+       if (fp_sensor_get_info(r, 1000) \u003c 0)\n #endif\n                return EC_RES_UNAVAILABLE;\n ```",
